WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.669 --> 00:00:07.610
When we think about Akainu, we directly think
about his notorious idea of absolute justice.

00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:10.670
But do we really know what that means?

00:00:10.670 --> 00:00:15.820
If absolute Justice means following the rules
without any question, wouldn´t that mean

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:21.430
that Akainu in his own eyes fails to act justly
when working with the warlords or confronting

00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:22.430
the Gorosei?

00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:27.380
No, there is actually a deeper meaning to
the principal of absolute justice.

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:30.199
And that is what we are going to explore together
today.

00:00:30.199 --> 00:00:36.359
A common misconception in storytelling, is
the idea that talking about a character is

00:00:36.359 --> 00:00:41.519
the same thing as talking about the person
that this character embodies in a story.

00:00:41.519 --> 00:00:47.049
You sometimes hear people talking about whether
a character is good or bad, based on the actions

00:00:47.049 --> 00:00:49.569
they take in relation to other characters.

00:00:49.569 --> 00:00:55.749
I think, most of you don´t need me to tell
you, that a good guy can be a bad character

00:00:55.749 --> 00:00:58.440
and that a bad guy can be a good one.

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:03.339
No matter if it´s Hollywood or the anime
world, anti-heroes and great villains have

00:01:03.339 --> 00:01:07.320
been a prominent element of storytelling for
quite some time now.

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:12.939
However, today, I want to talk about a different
misconception, that people seem to be less

00:01:12.939 --> 00:01:14.079
aware of.

00:01:14.079 --> 00:01:19.630
And that is the big issue of whether or not
it´s okay to like and enjoy an evil or morally

00:01:19.630 --> 00:01:21.920
questionable character.

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:26.890
As you know, taking a liking to the villain
of a story is a quite common thing, and yet

00:01:26.890 --> 00:01:31.890
often people get called out for enjoying a
character that clearly commits evil or at

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:34.090
least questionable acts.

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:39.009
How can you like Doflamingo, when he has committed
so many acts of violence and cruelty?

00:01:39.009 --> 00:01:42.749
I think all of you have had this experience
before.

00:01:42.749 --> 00:01:47.619
What often gets overlooked in this kind of
argument however is the fact that a character

00:01:47.619 --> 00:01:52.659
and the person they represent in their respective
world, are not the same thing.

00:01:52.659 --> 00:01:57.889
Liking a character and liking who that character
is are two fundamentally different things

00:01:57.889 --> 00:01:59.329
indeed.

00:01:59.329 --> 00:02:03.549
Liking the character implies liking the way
that character is designed and integrated

00:02:03.549 --> 00:02:04.860
into the story.

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:09.229
This is simply a question of good or bad writing.

00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:13.760
Liking a person in a story on the other hand
refers to liking their actions, their values

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:16.230
and their personality.

00:02:16.230 --> 00:02:20.630
Liking Doflamingo for being an excellent villain
to Luffy and bringing complexity and high

00:02:20.630 --> 00:02:25.989
stakes to the story is essentially different
from liking Doflamingo because he tyrannically

00:02:25.989 --> 00:02:28.580
rules and suppresses an entire country.

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:31.019
Do you see the point I´m trying to make here?

00:02:31.019 --> 00:02:36.500
So, when we talk about Akainu today, I want
you to be aware that I personally don´t agree

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:39.650
with his actions and his sense of justice
as a person.

00:02:39.650 --> 00:02:44.939
But I nonetheless think that he is an amazing
and great character, that I deeply enjoy seeing

00:02:44.939 --> 00:02:46.000
in the story.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:51.239
So, whatever your perspective on Akainu might
be, remember to distinguish between Akainu

00:02:51.239 --> 00:02:56.880
the character written for the story of One
Piece and Akainu the person acting in the

00:02:56.880 --> 00:02:58.190
world of One Piece.

00:02:58.190 --> 00:03:03.140
Therefore, we will first look at his character
and how he is written and then deconstruct

00:03:03.140 --> 00:03:07.530
what his sense of absolute justice represents
in the story.

00:03:07.530 --> 00:03:12.629
After all, being one of the central antagonists
of the series, Sakazuki doesn´t have a purely

00:03:12.629 --> 00:03:13.850
evil ideal.

00:03:13.850 --> 00:03:18.659
Oda simply takes his desire to bring down
the evil of the world and gives it a dark

00:03:18.659 --> 00:03:20.209
twist in perspective.

00:03:20.209 --> 00:03:27.319
This is the same principal he uses with Black
Beard, who like Luffy follows his ideal of

00:03:27.319 --> 00:03:28.319
dreams.

00:03:28.319 --> 00:03:32.950
Or like Doflamingo, who like White Beard follows
the ideal of family.

00:03:32.950 --> 00:03:38.250
According to Oda, the ideal you hold might
be good and just, but it is the practical

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:42.959
execution of this ideal that truly determines
who you are as a person.

00:03:42.959 --> 00:03:49.110
So, let´s find out what Akainu actually means
when he talks about absolute justice.

00:03:49.110 --> 00:03:54.440
Before we get into the steaming volcano of
personality, that is Sakazuki Akainu, though,

00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:57.640
a quick update on our small challenge.

00:03:57.640 --> 00:04:03.829
Once again you have reached the goal I set
you and gotten 3500 likes on Aokiji´s video.

00:04:03.829 --> 00:04:10.050
So, this time, I will raise the bar significantly
and challenge you to reach 4000 likes in the

00:04:10.050 --> 00:04:16.810
first 24 hours this video is online, and the
next admiral will be out within the week.

00:04:16.810 --> 00:04:22.090
But now, without any further a due, buckle
up, it´s about to get hot.

00:04:22.090 --> 00:04:29.600
Sakazuki Akainu is a muscular and broadly
built man that with over 3 meters in height,

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:34.130
is taller than any of the straw hats, including
even Jinbe.

00:04:34.130 --> 00:04:40.280
His design was based on the Japanese actor
Bunta Sugawara, with facial features strikingly

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:42.830
similar to his anime counterpart.

00:04:42.830 --> 00:04:47.820
In one of his movies, we can even see him
smoking a cigar and wearing the exact red

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:51.850
suit with the pink rose, that we know all
too well from Akainu.

00:04:51.850 --> 00:04:57.530
Additionally, Sakazuki also has a large tattoo
in the shape of a flower and flame pattern

00:04:57.530 --> 00:05:02.450
across his left chest and shoulder as well
as a small tattoo of a sword on his right

00:05:02.450 --> 00:05:07.150
arm, that might hint at the secret sword unit
inside the marines.

00:05:07.150 --> 00:05:13.850
Naturally, Akainu is also a physically strong
character, that also wields the powerful magma

00:05:13.850 --> 00:05:15.630
logia devil fruit.

00:05:15.630 --> 00:05:21.581
In fact, he is so strong, that Oda once even
stated in an interview that if he were to

00:05:21.581 --> 00:05:26.800
become the protagonist, he would be able end
the One Piece series within a single year.

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:30.330
Let that sink in for a second.

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:37.440
Born in the north blue, even as a child, Sakazuki
had a grim demeaner and a sense of justice.

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:42.290
He joined the marines around the same time
as his fellow admiral Borsalino and quickly

00:05:42.290 --> 00:05:45.250
rose in their ranks due to his notorious strength.

00:05:45.250 --> 00:05:51.290
A decisive moment in his past was the incident
of Ohara, that heavily shaped his idea of

00:05:51.290 --> 00:05:56.970
justice and set up the contrasting relationship
with his fellow admiral Aokiji.

00:05:56.970 --> 00:06:02.220
During the war at Marineford, he was the decisive
factor to win the war in favor of the marines.

00:06:02.220 --> 00:06:07.430
And later, after being victorious over Aokiji
in their duel, he rose to the position of

00:06:07.430 --> 00:06:09.380
fleet admiral.

00:06:09.380 --> 00:06:15.130
Putting morality and ethics aside, from a
purely militaristic perspective, his appointment

00:06:15.130 --> 00:06:17.090
made perfect sense.

00:06:17.090 --> 00:06:22.180
Being the one to ensure White Beards death
and carrying out Ace´s execution, he easily

00:06:22.180 --> 00:06:27.340
outperformed his two fellow admirals and even
the former fleet admiral Sengoku during the

00:06:27.340 --> 00:06:28.340
war.

00:06:28.340 --> 00:06:33.900
In the context of all these events, Oda depicts
Akainu as a hardline and almost extremist

00:06:33.900 --> 00:06:38.600
military leader, that in many ways hints at
the strict and brutal militaristic history

00:06:38.600 --> 00:06:43.550
of Japan, that is filled with warlords, shoguns
and generals.

00:06:43.550 --> 00:06:48.690
These were notoriously known for following
the values of their country, but in the process

00:06:48.690 --> 00:06:52.670
overlooking and stepping on the people they
were actually meant to protect in the first

00:06:52.670 --> 00:06:53.930
place.

00:06:53.930 --> 00:06:59.140
Outside of his duties, Akainu shows little
interest in anything besides conflict and

00:06:59.140 --> 00:07:00.150
war.

00:07:00.150 --> 00:07:05.150
Despite having a burning obsession to fulfill
his desire to eradicate all evil and end the

00:07:05.150 --> 00:07:12.000
pirate era, Sakazuki is a surprisingly level-headed
character who knows to contain himself and

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:14.020
not act impulsively.

00:07:14.020 --> 00:07:19.390
In fact, this sense of thoughtfulness and
cleverness makes his character so different

00:07:19.390 --> 00:07:23.390
from many other villains, that have a similar
basic design.

00:07:23.390 --> 00:07:28.500
Based on his appearance and his extreme believes,
one would expect Akainu to be an erratic and

00:07:28.500 --> 00:07:33.620
impulsive monster, that goes berserk whenever
something goes against his will or hurts his

00:07:33.620 --> 00:07:34.620
pride.

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:37.210
But just the opposite is the case.

00:07:37.210 --> 00:07:41.390
Akainu is surprisingly determined on thinking
things through.

00:07:41.390 --> 00:07:46.290
Not in the way Aokiji does of course, determining
who a person truly is and what a specific

00:07:46.290 --> 00:07:48.050
situation calls far.

00:07:48.050 --> 00:07:53.130
Akainu much rather determines how to get his
desired result in the most efficient and effective

00:07:53.130 --> 00:07:54.700
way possible.

00:07:54.700 --> 00:08:00.670
We can see this for instance when he manipulates
Squadro to attack White Beard or when he ruthlessly

00:08:00.670 --> 00:08:05.910
destroys a ship full of innocents on Ohara
to ensure the success of his mission.

00:08:05.910 --> 00:08:11.030
And of course, he also manipulates Ace into
taking him on one vs one, by taunting his

00:08:11.030 --> 00:08:15.760
beloved captain and in the end preventing
the pirates´ success.

00:08:15.760 --> 00:08:21.200
In close connection to this, Akainu also strongly
believes in thoroughness.

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:25.950
Based on his concept of absolute justice,
he swears by the idea that you have to finish

00:08:25.950 --> 00:08:30.690
what you started and IF you start it, you
have to go all the way.

00:08:30.690 --> 00:08:36.050
The best example of this is once again the
incident of Ohara, where after sacrificing

00:08:36.050 --> 00:08:56.149
a ship full of innocent civilians he states
the following: In other words, Akainu justifies

00:08:56.149 --> 00:09:02.399
his evil actions with the necessity for thoroughness
in the context of working for the greater

00:09:02.399 --> 00:09:03.399
good.

00:09:03.399 --> 00:09:07.440
A concept that you might be well familiar
with from the Harry Potter books.

00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:12.589
Finally, Akainu also has a strong sense of
pride.

00:09:12.589 --> 00:09:18.050
Pride in himself, but in extension also pride
in the institution of the marines and what

00:09:18.050 --> 00:09:20.180
they represent for the people.

00:09:20.180 --> 00:09:25.240
While he doesn´t feel the need to act honorable
in the face of pirates he can´t stand the

00:09:25.240 --> 00:09:30.180
idea of the marines failing to abide with
his absolute justice in the eye of the general

00:09:30.180 --> 00:09:31.180
population.

00:09:31.180 --> 00:09:36.310
That is why he is furious with Fujitora, who
shared with the world what had transpired

00:09:36.310 --> 00:09:39.640
on Dressrosa after Doflamingo´s defeat by
Luffy.

00:09:39.640 --> 00:09:46.110
Notably, next to Aokiji, we can also already
see a gaping hole between Akainu´s and Fujitora´s

00:09:46.110 --> 00:09:48.300
ideas of justice here.

00:09:48.300 --> 00:09:52.620
Most interestingly, however, is his anger
directed towards the Gorosei, when they try

00:09:52.620 --> 00:09:56.300
to cover up Doflamingo´s resignation from
the warlords.

00:09:56.300 --> 00:10:01.329
When they dismiss his concerns for the public
image of the marines, it becomes very clear

00:10:01.329 --> 00:10:06.250
that Akainu doesn´t agree with the notion
that the institution of the marines is nothing

00:10:06.250 --> 00:10:11.410
more than a mere a tool for the world government,
that can be used in any way they please.

00:10:11.410 --> 00:10:20.170
So now, based on this premise, let´s determine
what Akainu´s absolute Justice actually is.

00:10:20.170 --> 00:10:25.970
To learn, where Akainu´s perspective on justice
formed, we actually don´t have to speculate,

00:10:25.970 --> 00:10:28.980
but simply look at the master himself.

00:10:28.980 --> 00:10:35.509
Oda stated in an SBS that the idea of absolute
justice stems from Sakazuki´s decision to

00:10:35.509 --> 00:10:40.519
burn down Robin's homeland Ohara completely
without any chance for survivors in order

00:10:40.519 --> 00:10:42.000
to demolish all evil.

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:48.149
I think this is extremely interesting, since
it not only suggests, that Akainu was not

00:10:48.149 --> 00:10:53.259
as determined before the incident, but also
because it shows us how the same impactful

00:10:53.259 --> 00:10:59.399
event has brought two initially not so different
people to morally opposite sides of the same

00:10:59.399 --> 00:11:00.699
spectrum.

00:11:00.699 --> 00:11:05.220
Being confronted with the extreme brutality
of the buster call, Akainu coped with it by

00:11:05.220 --> 00:11:11.120
justifying it with the need to always be absolute
and thorough, while Aokiji decided to go against

00:11:11.120 --> 00:11:14.980
his superiors and fulfill his own moral justice.

00:11:14.980 --> 00:11:20.030
Based on this, Akainu´s idea of justice seems
to compel him to always follow the law, with

00:11:20.030 --> 00:11:24.089
no regard for the situation or the people
involved.

00:11:24.089 --> 00:11:25.569
Rules are rules.

00:11:25.569 --> 00:11:30.140
There are no exceptions and no second chances.

00:11:30.140 --> 00:11:34.850
Sakazuki follows this credo in the believe
that it is the only way to end the root of

00:11:34.850 --> 00:11:36.399
all evil in the world.

00:11:36.399 --> 00:11:38.370
The great pirate era.

00:11:38.370 --> 00:11:44.129
As a result, he has definitely heavily contributed
to the marine’s success in the past.

00:11:44.129 --> 00:11:49.019
Being the decisive factor in the war, his
wits and ruthlessness were two major factors

00:11:49.019 --> 00:11:53.129
in defeating White Beard and finishing Ace´s
execution.

00:11:53.129 --> 00:11:57.160
Part of that is also his strong believe in
the meaning of bloodlines.

00:11:57.160 --> 00:12:03.139
While Aokiji looks at a person’s actions,
Akainu judges a person's heritage as an indicator

00:12:03.139 --> 00:12:05.550
for how big of a threat they pose.

00:12:05.550 --> 00:12:11.001
We can see this in the intensity with which
he goes against Ace, the son of the pirate

00:12:11.001 --> 00:12:15.320
king and against Luffy, the son of the most
wanted man in the world.

00:12:15.320 --> 00:12:20.850
All these examples show us the contrast between
the soft and liberal Aokiji and the strict

00:12:20.850 --> 00:12:23.199
and conservative Akainu.

00:12:23.199 --> 00:12:27.600
When looking at these decisions, one could
possibly find an argument, that Sakazuki is

00:12:27.600 --> 00:12:32.509
simply a hard-liner that takes drastic action
in a suffering world.

00:12:32.509 --> 00:12:38.750
However, as we all know, Akainu is also responsible
for some horrendous and extreme actions, by

00:12:38.750 --> 00:12:43.310
which Oda puts him in the clear category of
an antagonist.

00:12:43.310 --> 00:12:47.459
One of the most prominent examples of this
is of course the killing of innocent civilians

00:12:47.459 --> 00:12:49.279
on Ohara out of a whim.

00:12:49.279 --> 00:12:54.029
A decision that he made on his own and not
based on orders.

00:12:54.029 --> 00:12:58.740
Another example would be him pushing for the
complete annihilation of the pirates during

00:12:58.740 --> 00:13:04.370
the war, not caring for the suffering of his
own men and their desire to stop the killing.

00:13:04.370 --> 00:13:10.160
In a way the worst example of this, however,
is the execution of his own men for refusing

00:13:10.160 --> 00:13:13.639
an order, without any chance for a trial.

00:13:13.639 --> 00:13:20.620
This has nothing to do with justice or thoroughness
but is simply an act of tyranny and cruelty.

00:13:20.620 --> 00:13:25.509
We can see this behavior again, when Coby
dares to stand up to him during the war, his

00:13:25.509 --> 00:13:28.620
sentence barely being stopped by Shanks.

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:34.160
These examples show us very well, how the
wrong take on the right ideal can create suffering

00:13:34.160 --> 00:13:37.819
for those that were meant to be protected
by it in the first place.

00:13:37.819 --> 00:13:43.970
Sacrificing civilians and soldiers alike just
to get the job done, is not what justice is

00:13:43.970 --> 00:13:45.290
about.

00:13:45.290 --> 00:13:50.430
What is even more interesting to me, however,
is that Akainu´s justice might actually not

00:13:50.430 --> 00:13:52.519
even be that absolute after all.

00:13:52.519 --> 00:13:58.199
There are a number of things that should clearly
violate the idea of absoluteness.

00:13:58.199 --> 00:14:03.050
Working with the warlords, in other words
pirates, should be impossible under Akainu´s

00:14:03.050 --> 00:14:04.329
idea of justice.

00:14:04.329 --> 00:14:07.220
Yet he does it, to make use of their strength.

00:14:07.220 --> 00:14:12.740
Ignoring Wano and not moving against the Yonko
should be a no-go when you want to be thorough.

00:14:12.740 --> 00:14:17.619
But he decides against it, well knowing that
his forces might not be sufficient.

00:14:17.619 --> 00:14:22.649
Arguing with Fujitora that coverups are necessary,
while the existence of coverup´s themselves

00:14:22.649 --> 00:14:25.439
should be impossible under his vision.

00:14:25.439 --> 00:14:30.190
Letting Aokiji go after their duel out of
respect, while brutally executing a random

00:14:30.190 --> 00:14:31.610
foot soldier.

00:14:31.610 --> 00:14:36.779
And last but not least opposing the Gorosei
and world nobles, while at the same time supporting

00:14:36.779 --> 00:14:42.649
their system of slavery, racism, exploitation
and undisputed dominance of the weak.

00:14:42.649 --> 00:14:48.399
How can you justify these actions, when your
ideal is the absolute nature of rules?

00:14:48.399 --> 00:14:52.260
The answer to that is as surprising as it
is simple.

00:14:52.260 --> 00:14:56.930
Akainu´s justice claims to be absolute in
regard to the rules of the world.

00:14:56.930 --> 00:15:01.310
But it is actually based on his own set of
ideals and values.

00:15:01.310 --> 00:15:07.790
So, in the end, he and Aokiji both ended up
following their own sense of justice, while

00:15:07.790 --> 00:15:11.779
taking opposite paths after the destruction
of Ohara.

00:15:11.779 --> 00:15:16.709
Both want to achieve justice at heart and
are opposed to the actions of the world government.

00:15:16.709 --> 00:15:21.939
And yet they are as different as it gets in
their execution of this ideal.

00:15:21.939 --> 00:15:26.519
What all of this leaves us with now, is the
hidden moral need that Oda has given Akainu

00:15:26.519 --> 00:15:28.399
for his future conflict with Luffy.

00:15:28.399 --> 00:15:35.069
The need to understand that evil isn't determined
by your blood or affiliation, but much rather

00:15:35.069 --> 00:15:39.319
by who you are as a person and whether your
actions hurt those around you.

00:15:39.319 --> 00:15:43.660
And even though he has lost his path, I am
sure he will get there.

00:15:43.660 --> 00:15:48.860
After all, in his heart, Akainu is burning
for true justice.

00:15:48.860 --> 00:15:51.730
I hope you guys enjoyed this video.

00:15:51.730 --> 00:15:54.470
If you did don´t forget to hit that like
button.

00:15:54.470 --> 00:15:57.939
And make sure to subscribe, if you aren´t
part of the crew yet.

00:15:57.939 --> 00:16:05.110
The winner of last week´s title contest for
Aokiji is Matthew Kwon with the Aokiji Coolzan.

00:16:05.110 --> 00:16:06.720
I love it.

00:16:06.720 --> 00:16:09.990
But I also saw many other great ideas!

00:16:09.990 --> 00:16:12.230
Make sure to share your version for Akainu.

00:16:12.230 --> 00:16:15.560
I´m curious what you can come up with.

00:16:15.560 --> 00:16:19.730
